            <section class="my-8 py-2">
                <RzHeading Level="HeadingLevel.H2" QuickReferenceTitle="Accessibility" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    Accessibility
                </RzHeading>
                <RzParagraph>
                    RzAccordion follows the WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices Guide accordion pattern. Each item exposes a real <code>button</code> inside a semantic heading, and the button controls a panel with stable ID-based relationships.
                </RzParagraph>
                <ul>
                    <li>Each trigger uses <code>aria-expanded</code> to reflect the current open state.</li>
                    <li>Each trigger uses <code>aria-controls</code> to reference its panel ID.</li>
                    <li>Each panel uses <code>role=&quot;region&quot;</code> and <code>aria-labelledby</code> to reference its trigger ID.</li>
                    <li>The accordion container does not add a composite widget role, so Tab order remains the browser's natural button order.</li>
                </ul>

                <RzHeading Level="HeadingLevel.H3" QuickReferenceTitle="Keyboard behavior" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    Keyboard behavior
                </RzHeading>
                <div class="not-prose mt-6 mb-10 overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800">
