                        </thead>
                        <tbody class="divide-y divide-zinc-200 dark:divide-zinc-800">
                            <tr class="align-top">
                                <td class="px-4 py-4"><code class="font-mono font-medium text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">Enter</code></td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-4 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Activates the focused trigger button and toggles its panel through native button behavior.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr class="align-top">
                                <td class="px-4 py-4"><code class="font-mono font-medium text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">Space</code></td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-4 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Activates the focused trigger button and toggles its panel through native button behavior.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr class="align-top">
                                <td class="px-4 py-4"><code class="font-mono font-medium text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">ArrowDown</code></td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-4 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Moves focus to the next enabled accordion trigger, wrapping to the first trigger.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr class="align-top">
                                <td class="px-4 py-4"><code class="font-mono font-medium text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">ArrowUp</code></td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-4 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Moves focus to the previous enabled accordion trigger, wrapping to the last trigger.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr class="align-top">
                                <td class="px-4 py-4"><code class="font-mono font-medium text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">Home</code></td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-4 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Moves focus to the first enabled accordion trigger.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr class="align-top">
                                <td class="px-4 py-4"><code class="font-mono font-medium text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">End</code></td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-4 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Moves focus to the last enabled accordion trigger.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr class="align-top">
                                <td class="px-4 py-4"><code class="font-mono font-medium text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">Tab</code></td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-4 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Moves through triggers and focusable panel content in normal document order.</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <RzHeading Level="HeadingLevel.H3" QuickReferenceTitle="Focus, announcements, and SSR" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    Focus, announcements, and SSR
                </RzHeading>
                <RzParagraph>
                    Opening or closing a panel preserves focus on the trigger that was activated. Arrow, Home, and End keys only move focus between triggers and do not change the open state. No live region announcements are emitted because the trigger's <code>aria-expanded</code> state and panel relationship provide the state change to assistive technologies without additional noise.
                </RzParagraph>
                <RzParagraph>
                    RzAccordion is SSR-only and CSP-compatible. The initial <code>aria-expanded</code> value is rendered in HTML from the <code>Collapsed</code> parameter, and Alpine updates the same attribute after hydration. The default and CSP runtimes keep the existing <code>rzAccordion</code> and <code>accordionItem</code> component names in the <code>core-common</code> bundle.
                </RzParagraph>
                <RzParagraph>
                    Known limitation: the optional arrow-key navigation only moves between enabled triggers rendered inside the same accordion root. Custom trigger content should not place additional interactive controls inside the trigger button, because nested interactive controls are invalid HTML and can produce inconsistent assistive technology behavior.
                </RzParagraph>
